# PrivateMesh public demo — environment. Copy to `demo.env` next to this file (gitignored; never
# commit the copy) before `docker compose -f deploy/demo/compose.yaml up`.
#
# Every default below is the SAME safe default `demo_session.DemoCaps.from_env` already falls back
# to for a missing/unreadable/zero/negative/above-ceiling value — this file does not invent a
# separate policy, it documents the one the code enforces. All are comfortably inside this lane's
# ceiling (whole-demo total <= $3.00, daily <= $0.50): the code's own defaults are $1.00 total /
# $0.25 daily, tighter than required. See docs/API_V2.md, "The public demo", and
# src/privatemesh/demo_session.py for the absolute ceiling each setting cannot be raised past
# (a value past its ceiling is treated as unreadable and falls back to the default, same as a typo).
#
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE: NEBIUS_API_KEY, TAVILY_API_KEY, and any Google credential
# (GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS / a token under the Google token directory). The model key is
# injected at container start from a docker secret file (see compose.yaml, PM_NEBIUS_API_KEY_FILE)
# and must never appear in this file or any committed one. The other two must never be set on this
# host at all: `wiring.build_demo` -> `demo_session.refuse_if_providers_configured` refuses to start
# the process the moment either is present, by design — see README.md, "It refuses to start beside
# a real credential", and tests/test_demo_mode.py::
#   test_demo_refuses_to_start_when_a_real_provider_credential_is_configured
#   test_a_google_token_on_disk_is_also_a_real_provider_credential
#   test_serve_demo_refuses_to_start_while_a_real_credential_is_present

# --- one visitor's own budget -----------------------------------------------------------------
# What one visitor's model calls may cost. Ceiling $1.00.
PM_DEMO_SESSION_USD=0.05
# How many model calls one visitor may make. Ceiling 50.
PM_DEMO_SESSION_CALLS=24
# One client's requests per PM_DEMO_RATE_WINDOW seconds (a token bucket). Ceiling 600.
PM_DEMO_RATE_REQUESTS=10
PM_DEMO_RATE_WINDOW=60
# The bounded table backing the rate limiter — how many distinct clients it tracks. Ceiling 4096.
PM_DEMO_RATE_MAX_CALLERS=512

# --- the whole demo's budget, across every visitor --------------------------------------------
# Ceilings $5.00 / $1.00 — kept here at half the lane's own caps ($3.00 / $0.50) so there is
# headroom under the lane cap even if a setting is ever raised without this file being re-read.
PM_DEMO_TOTAL_USD=1.00
PM_DEMO_DAILY_USD=0.25

# --- session bookkeeping -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# How many visitor sessions may be live at once, and how long an idle one lives. Ceilings 4096 /
# 86400 (a day).
PM_DEMO_MAX_SESSIONS=256
PM_DEMO_SESSION_TTL=1800

# --- the one process the caps above are true for -------------------------------------------------
# `wiring.build_demo` calls `demo_session.refuse_if_multi_worker`, which reads this name (then
# WEB_CONCURRENCY, UVICORN_WORKERS, GUNICORN_WORKERS, WORKERS — first one present wins) and
# REFUSES TO START on anything but 1 or nothing declared. The session table, the rate buckets and
# the ledger are all held in one process's memory, so N workers would silently serve N times the
# caps this file prints. `1` here is the same thing as leaving it unset — it is written out so the
# name appears in this file at all, not because the deploy needs it. Removing it is safe; setting
# it to anything else (including an unreadable value like `auto`) stops the API on purpose.
PM_DEMO_WORKERS=1

# --- where the whole-demo ledger lives ----------------------------------------------------------
# compose.yaml sets this to a path under the named `demo_ledger` volume — do not point it outside
# that volume, or the whole-demo total/daily caps reset every time the container restarts.
PM_DEMO_LEDGER=/home/privatemesh/.privatemesh/demo-spend.db

# --- optional: model routing --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Demo mode already falls back to the measured, working model ids in
# `wiring.DEMO_MODEL_DEFAULTS` when these are unset — set them only to point at a different
# deployment on the same Token Factory account. Never a secret; these are public model identifiers.
#PM_MODEL_FAST=nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3-Nano-30B-A3B
#PM_MODEL_REASON=nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b
#PM_MODEL_DEEP=nvidia/Nemotron-3-Ultra-550b-a55b

# --- optional: CORS ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed if something calls the API from a browser on a DIFFERENT origin than the one Caddy
# serves it from. compose.yaml's own Caddyfile puts the web build and the API under one origin
# (`/api/*` vs everything else), so the default (blank -> local dev pair only) is normally correct.
#PM_WEB_ORIGINS=

# --- the public hostname Caddy serves ------------------------------------------------------------
# Compose reads this one DIFFERENTLY from every setting above, so it is commented out and NOT set
# here: `compose.yaml`'s caddy service gets `PM_DEMO_DOMAIN: ${PM_DEMO_DOMAIN:-localhost}`, and the
# `${...}` is compose INTERPOLATION — resolved from the shell environment (or a `.env` next to the
# compose file), never from this `demo.env`, which reaches only the `api` service via `env_file`.
# A live `PM_DEMO_DOMAIN=` line in this file would therefore look like it configured Caddy while
# doing nothing to it. Set it on the command line instead, as docs/DEPLOY.md does:
#   PM_DEMO_DOMAIN=your-demo-hostname.example docker compose -f deploy/demo/compose.yaml up -d
# `localhost` (compose's own default when unset) is what the local proof run uses: Caddy treats a
# non-public name as internal and serves TLS from its own CA, no ACME. A real public hostname with
# DNS already pointed at the VM makes Caddy request a Let's Encrypt certificate on first boot.
#PM_DEMO_DOMAIN=your-demo-hostname.example
